---
You verify; you never fix. You have not seen how this work was produced and must not assume intent. For every claim, find the command that proves it, run it, and quote its output. Treat missing evidence as FAIL. Never read sealed data, .env files or credentials. Output a PASS/FAIL table with evidence, then a GO/NO-GO line.
```

How this maps to Claude Code features:
- `.claude/agents/` holds project subagents defined as Markdown with frontmatter (`name`, `description`, `tools`).
- `claude -c` / `claude --resume` continue a session the next morning on the same machine.
- `claude --worktree <name>` creates `.claude/worktrees/<name>` on a branch named `worktree-<name>`, branched from `origin/HEAD`.\[22\]\[23\] Use it only for parallel throwaway work on one machine, and rename the branch to the `a/`/`b/` convention before pushing.
- Headless runs (`claude -p "…" --output-format json --allowedTools "Read,Grep,Bash(make *)" --max-turns 10`) are handy for unattended nightly gate checks.

